note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note seed/ng/gate-ir.om: the M0 gate of the ΩIR spec and its tools (seed/ng/IR.md). Owner: ng-ir lane.
note Build: cat seed/ng/sha256.om seed/ng/gate-ir.om | seed/out/omc > gate-ir
note Run from the repository root: gate-ir OMC SCRATCH   (SCRATCH is created if absent)
note 1. builds ngbuild, ngcheck, ngas, ngdis and ngrun with OMC, then ng through `ngbuild build` (pins of ng.units)
note 2. `ngcheck --table` must equal seed/ng/hostwords.tsv byte for byte
note 3. ngbuild refuses a units file with a wrong pin (exit 3, the exact mismatch line) before compiling
note 4. every line of seed/ng/tests/ir/cases (format in that file): text round trip ngdis(ngas(t)) == t,
note    ngcheck's whole witness line (ACCEPT, sha256 of the binary by sha256.om, fns/blocks/ops counted
note    from the fixture text) or whole refusal line with empty stdout, ng ir-copy on every unit (IR.md
note    s14), ngas syntax and limit refusals, byte mutants judged by ngcheck, ngdis and ng, an unreadable
note    stdin, generated inputs at the capacities (16777216 bytes and one more, 65537 table entries), and
note    run pairs (D9 differential): NAME.oir, which ngcheck must accept, run by ngrun, against NAME.om
note    compiled by OMC; exit status, stdout and stderr must be equal
note 5. negative controls of the gate itself: a wrong exit, a wrong offset and a wrong round-trip text
note    must each trip their named check ("FAIL negative control N" otherwise).
note 6. three tool mutants of ngcheck (gt_msel: load/store typing away, witness prefix, class name) and
note    one of ngrun (chk.fuel one pass late) must each fail their named check at least once ("ok mutant
note    ...: killed by=K" counts those failures; "FAIL mutant ...: named failure never fired" otherwise).
note Output: one line per failure, then "NGIRGATE PASS cases=N" (exit 0) or "NGIRGATE FAIL failed=K
note cases=N" (exit 1); usage or scratch failure exit 2, a tool that does not build exit 3.
note Globals q_*, functions gt_*; sha256.om supplies sh_dat, sh_all, sh_dig.
text q_w "seed/ng/ ngbuild ngcheck ngas ngdis ng sha256.om ngbuild.om ngcheck.om ngtxt.om ngas.om ngdis.om ng.units hostwords.tsv tests/ir/ cases .oir build --table src.om out err in bin txt tests/ir unit bad.units nope must src/ir.om ngrun ngrun.om .om ref rout rerr "
text q_m "FAIL |build|table|case|: ngas exit|: ngdis exit|: round trip text differs|: ngcheck exit|: offset|: ACCEPT digest|: ir-copy exit|: ir-copy bytes differ|: ngas syntax line|: malformed case|negative control |NGIRGATE PASS cases=|NGIRGATE FAIL failed=| cases=|usage: gate-ir OMC SCRATCH|scratch unusable|: ngdis exit|: unreadable fixture|mutant ngcheck: |survived every case|not built|killed by=|ok |ngcheck: |ngdis: refused class |ng: refused class |ngas: syntax error at line |ngas: limit at line | at |ACCEPT | fns=| blocks=| ops=|: witness line differs|: refusal line differs|: refusal wrote stdout|: ng exit|bad pin: |not refused before compiling, exit|mutant ngcheck ACCEPT prefix: |mutant ngcheck class name: |: unknown generator|ngbuild: sha256 mismatch seed/ng/src/ir.om have |named failure never fired, other failures=|fn |export |kernel |block |end|omegair 1\n|type %t| = array u8 |type %t32 = array u8 1\n|global @g| %t32 zero\n|fn @f| flags 0 -> void\nblock ^0\nret %0\nend\n|fn @f0 flags 0 -> void\nblock ^0\n|ret %0\n|block ^| %|:tok\nret %|fn @f0 flags 0|:u32| -> void\nblock ^0\nret %0\nend\n|br ^1 %0\nblock ^1 %1:tok|\nret %1\nend\n|end\n|full|over|types|ty65536|ty65537|gl65537|fn65537|bl65537|fp65537|bp65537|: generated input differs|OSC1IR|omega.ng.ir.v1|: named check never fired|mutant ngrun: |: run exits differ, ngrun |, reference |: run stdout differs|: run stderr differs|: reference build|ngrun: refused class |"
note the tool mutants of ngcheck (each pattern occurs once; the replacement has its length):
note 1 load and store typing dispatched away, 2 the witness prints " ops=" for "ACCEPT ",
note 3 a refusal names the class after the right one
text q_mu0 "\nif or eq op 42 eq op 43\n"
text q_mu1 "\nif or eq op 99 eq op 99\n"
text q_mp0 "\nck_txt 3 1\n"
text q_mp1 "\nck_txt 6 1\n"
text q_mc0 "\nck_cname sub c 9\n"
text q_mc1 "\nck_cname sub c 8\n"
note the ngrun mutant (id 4): chk.fuel fails one pass late
text q_mu2 "\nif eq op 81\nret ge a b\n"
text q_mu3 "\nif eq op 81\nret gt a b\n"
note the IR.md s11 class names of exits 10..30, in order (the gate's own copy)
text q_cn "MAGIC VERSION TRUNCATED NONCANONICAL TRAILING UNKNOWN_OP TYPE USE_BEFORE_DEF DOMINANCE BLOCK_ARITY UNTERMINATED CHECK_CODE EFFECT LIMIT REF UNCHECKED UNREACHABLE IO TOKEN FACT ENTRY "
text q_irc "@ng ir-copy\n"
text q_hex "0123456789abcdef"
global q_wo uint 64
global q_wl uint 64
global q_mo uint 128
global q_ml uint 128
global q_omc uchar 4096
global q_scr uchar 4096
global q_pa uchar 8192
global q_av uchar 16384
global q_b1 uchar 16777216
global q_b2 uchar 16777216
global q_cs uchar 1048576
global q_o uchar 4096
global q_stb uchar 4
global q_n ulong 32
global q_co uint 32
global q_cl uint 32
global q_fk ulong 128
global q_ex uchar 4096
global q_ma uchar 64
global q_mb uchar 64
note q_n: 0 path length, 1 omc length, 2 scratch length (with '/'), 3 argv bytes, 4 argc,
note 5 b1 length, 6 b2 length, 7 cases length, 8 cases cursor, 9 out length, 10 cases run,
note 11 failures, 12 current case failed, 13 case line start, 14 control mode, 15 expected exit,
note 16 expected offset (or line), 17 offset present, 18 last child exit, 19 name end, 20 mutant id,
note 21 expected line length (q_ex), 22..24 fixture fns, blocks, ops, 25 mutant pattern length,
note 26 generator cursor in b1; q_fk counts failures by message (named kills and controls)
note ---- words, output ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn gt_init to void
w = ulong 0
s = ulong 0
for i ulong len q_w
if eq get q_w i 32
put q_wo w uint s
put q_wl w uint sub i s
w = add w 1
s = add i 1
end
end
w = 0
s = 0
for i ulong len q_cn
if eq get q_cn i 32
put q_co w uint s
put q_cl w uint sub i s
w = add w 1
s = add i 1
end
end
w = 0
s = 0
for i ulong len q_m
if eq get q_m i 124
put q_mo w uint s
put q_ml w uint sub i s
w = add w 1
s = add i 1
end
end
end
fn gt_c b ulong to void
n = get q_n 9
if lt n len q_o
put q_o n uchar b
put q_n 9 add n 1
end
end
fn gt_nl to void
gt_c 10
r = write 1 q_o 0 get q_n 9
put q_n 9 0
end
fn gt_say i ulong to void
s = ulong get q_mo i
for j ulong ulong get q_ml i bound 64
gt_c ulong get q_m add s j
end
end
fn gt_num v ulong to void
if ge v 10
gt_num div v 10
end
gt_c add 48 rem v 10
end
note echo the current case line
fn gt_line to void
p = get q_n 13
while lt p get q_n 7 bound 4096
c = ulong get q_cs p
if eq c 10
ret
end
gt_c c
p = add p 1
end
end
note a failure of the current case: FAIL <case line><message i>[ value]
fn gt_fail i ulong to void
put q_n 12 1
put q_fk i add get q_fk i 1
if ne get q_n 14 0
ret
end
gt_say 0
gt_line
gt_say i
end
fn gt_failv i ulong v ulong to void
gt_fail i
if eq get q_n 14 0
gt_c 32
gt_num v
gt_nl
end
end
fn gt_fail0 i ulong to void
gt_fail i
if eq get q_n 14 0
gt_nl
end
end
note ---- paths ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn gt_pclr to void
put q_n 0 0
end
fn gt_pc c ulong to void
n = get q_n 0
put q_pa n uchar c
put q_n 0 add n 1
end
fn gt_pw i ulong to void
s = ulong get q_wo i
for j ulong ulong get q_wl i bound 64
gt_pc ulong get q_w add s j
end
end
note scratch file word i
fn gt_ps i ulong to void
gt_pclr
for j ulong get q_n 2 bound 4096
gt_pc ulong get q_scr j
end
gt_pw i
end
note repository file seed/ng/ + word i
fn gt_pr i ulong to void
gt_pclr
gt_pw 0
gt_pw i
end
note fixture seed/ng/tests/ir/<name>.oir, the name at cases [a, b)
fn gt_pfix a ulong b ulong to void
gt_pfx a b 16
end
note fixture seed/ng/tests/ir/<name><word w>
fn gt_pfx a ulong b ulong w ulong to void
gt_pclr
gt_pw 0
gt_pw 14
for j ulong sub b a bound 256
gt_pc ulong get q_cs add a j
end
gt_pw w
end
fn gt_open fl ulong to int
r = fopen q_pa 0 get q_n 0 int fl 420
if lt r 0
ret -1
end
ret int r
end
fn gt_rdonly to int
ret gt_open 524288
end
fn gt_wronly to int
ret gt_open 524865
end
note ---- whole files ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
note read the file at q_pa into b1 (k 1) or b2 (k 2); false when unreadable or larger than the buffer
fn gt_slurp k ulong to bool
fd = gt_rdonly
if lt fd 0
ret false
end
n = ulong 0
ok = true
while true bound 16777218
x = long 0
if eq k 1
x = read fd q_b1 n sub len q_b1 n
else
x = read fd q_b2 n sub len q_b2 n
end
if lt x 0
ok = false
break
end
if eq x 0
break
end
n = add n ulong x
if ge n len q_b1
ok = false
break
end
end
r = fclose fd
put q_n add 4 k n
ret ok
end
note write b1[0, n) to the file at q_pa
fn gt_spill n ulong to bool
fd = gt_wronly
if lt fd 0
ret false
end
o = ulong 0
while lt o n bound 16777217
x = write fd q_b1 o sub n o
if le x 0
r = fclose fd
ret false
end
o = add o ulong x
end
r = fclose fd
ret true
end
fn gt_same to bool
n = get q_n 5
if ne n get q_n 6
ret false
end
for j ulong n bound 16777216
if ne get q_b1 j get q_b2 j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note ---- children -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn gt_aclr to void
put q_n 3 2
put q_n 4 0
end
fn gt_aend n ulong to void
p = get q_n 3
put q_av p uchar and n 255
put q_av add p 1 uchar shr n 8
put q_n 3 add p add n 2
c = add get q_n 4 1
put q_n 4 c
put q_av 0 uchar and c 255
put q_av 1 uchar shr c 8
end
note append q_pa as the next argument
fn gt_apa to void
p = add get q_n 3 2
n = get q_n 0
for j ulong n bound 8192
put q_av add p j get q_pa j
end
gt_aend n
end
note append word i as the next argument
fn gt_aw i ulong to void
gt_pclr
gt_pw i
gt_apa
end
note run the argument list with stdin, stdout, stderr fds; the exit code, 256 + signal byte otherwise
fn gt_spawn fi int fo int fe int to ulong
if or lt fi 0 or lt fo 0 lt fe 0
gt_fclo fi
gt_fclo fo
gt_fclo fe
ret 512
end
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
exit 2
end
if eq pid 0
gt_redir fi 0
gt_redir fo 1
gt_redir fe 2
r = execprog q_av 0 get q_n 3
exit 127
end
gt_fclo fi
gt_fclo fo
gt_fclo fe
r = waitpid int pid q_stb 0 len q_stb 0
if ne r pid
exit 2
end
x = ulong get q_stb 0
if ne x 0
ret add 256 x
end
v = ulong get q_stb 1
put q_n 18 v
ret v
end
fn gt_redir s int d int to void
if ne dupfd s d 0 long d
exit 127
end
end
fn gt_fclo fd int to void
if ge fd 0
r = fclose fd
end
end
note run tool word t (built in scratch) with no argument, stdin from the path in q_pa,
note stdout to scratch word o, stderr to scratch err
fn gt_tool t ulong o ulong to ulong
fi = gt_rdonly
gt_aclr
gt_ps t
gt_apa
gt_ps o
fo = gt_wronly
gt_ps 21
fe = gt_wronly
ret gt_spawn fi fo fe
end
note ---- build ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note concatenate seed/ng/<a> and seed/ng/<b> into scratch src.om, compile it with OMC to scratch <o>
fn gt_build a ulong b ulong o ulong to bool
gt_pr a
if not gt_slurp 1
ret false
end
n = get q_n 5
gt_pr b
if not gt_slurp 2
ret false
end
m = get q_n 6
if gt add n m len q_b1
ret false
end
for j ulong m bound 16777216
put q_b1 add n j get q_b2 j
end
if ne get q_n 20 0
if not gt_mutate add n m
ret false
end
end
gt_ps 19
if not gt_spill add n m
ret false
end
ret gt_bodyb o
end
note apply mutant q_n 20 (its pattern q_ma -> q_mb) at its one place in b1[0, n)
fn gt_mutate n ulong to bool
gt_msel get q_n 20
k = get q_n 25
for p ulong n bound 16777216
if gt_mat p k
for j ulong k bound 64
put q_b1 add p j get q_mb j
end
ret true
end
end
ret false
end
fn gt_mat p ulong k ulong to bool
for j ulong k bound 64
if ne get q_b1 add p j get q_ma j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note pattern and replacement of mutant id into q_ma, q_mb (length q_n 25)
fn gt_msel id ulong to void
if eq id 1
put q_n 25 len q_mu0
for j ulong len q_mu0 bound 64
put q_ma j get q_mu0 j
put q_mb j get q_mu1 j
end
end
if eq id 2
put q_n 25 len q_mp0
for j ulong len q_mp0 bound 64
put q_ma j get q_mp0 j
put q_mb j get q_mp1 j
end
end
if eq id 3
put q_n 25 len q_mc0
for j ulong len q_mc0 bound 64
put q_ma j get q_mc0 j
put q_mb j get q_mc1 j
end
end
if eq id 4
put q_n 25 len q_mu2
for j ulong len q_mu2 bound 64
put q_ma j get q_mu2 j
put q_mb j get q_mu3 j
end
end
end
fn gt_bodyb o ulong to bool
fi = gt_rdonly
gt_aclr
gt_pclr
for j ulong get q_n 1 bound 4096
gt_pc ulong get q_omc j
end
gt_apa
gt_ps o
fo = gt_exe
gt_ps 21
fe = gt_wronly
ret eq gt_spawn fi fo fe 0
end
note open scratch q_pa for writing with mode 0755 (created fresh: unlink first)
fn gt_exe to int
r = unlink q_pa 0 get q_n 0
x = fopen q_pa 0 get q_n 0 524865 493
if lt x 0
ret -1
end
ret int x
end
fn gt_tools to bool
if not gt_build 6 7 1
ret false
end
if not gt_build 6 8 2
ret false
end
if not gt_build 9 10 3
ret false
end
if not gt_build 9 11 4
ret false
end
if not gt_build 30 32 31
ret false
end
note ng through ngbuild: ngbuild build OMC seed/ng/ng.units SCRATCH/ng
gt_aclr
gt_ps 1
gt_apa
gt_aw 17
gt_pclr
for j ulong get q_n 1 bound 4096
gt_pc ulong get q_omc j
end
gt_apa
gt_pr 12
gt_apa
gt_ps 5
gt_apa
gt_pr 12
fi = gt_rdonly
gt_ps 20
fo = gt_wronly
gt_ps 21
fe = gt_wronly
ret eq gt_spawn fi fo fe 0
end
fn gt_table to bool
gt_aclr
gt_ps 2
gt_apa
gt_aw 18
gt_pr 12
fi = gt_rdonly
gt_ps 20
fo = gt_wronly
gt_ps 21
fe = gt_wronly
if ne gt_spawn fi fo fe 0
ret false
end
gt_ps 20
if not gt_slurp 1
ret false
end
gt_pr 13
if not gt_slurp 2
ret false
end
ret gt_same
end
note ---- cases parsing -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn gt_pk to ulong
p = get q_n 8
if ge p get q_n 7
ret 10
end
ret ulong get q_cs p
end
fn gt_adv to void
put q_n 8 add get q_n 8 1
end
fn gt_skip to void
while eq gt_pk 32 bound 4096
gt_adv
end
end
note a decimal field; q_n 17 = 0 when the field is "-" or absent (value 0)
fn gt_dec to ulong
gt_skip
put q_n 17 0
if eq gt_pk 45
gt_adv
ret 0
end
v = ulong 0
while and ge gt_pk 48 le gt_pk 57 bound 20
v = add mul v 10 sub gt_pk 48
gt_adv
put q_n 17 1
end
ret v
end
note a name field: its start; its end goes to q_n 19
fn gt_name to ulong
gt_skip
a = get q_n 8
while and ne gt_pk 32 ne gt_pk 10 bound 256
gt_adv
end
put q_n 19 get q_n 8
ret a
end
fn gt_eol to void
while ne gt_pk 10 bound 4096
gt_adv
end
gt_adv
end
note ---- checks ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note the expected stdout or stderr line is built in q_ex (length q_n 21)
fn gt_xclr to void
put q_n 21 0
end
fn gt_xc c ulong to void
n = get q_n 21
if lt n len q_ex
put q_ex n uchar c
put q_n 21 add n 1
end
end
fn gt_xs i ulong to void
s = ulong get q_mo i
for j ulong ulong get q_ml i bound 128
gt_xc ulong get q_m add s j
end
end
fn gt_xnum v ulong to void
if ge v 10
gt_xnum div v 10
end
gt_xc add 48 rem v 10
end
note the class name of exit c (10..30), its number otherwise
fn gt_xcn c ulong to void
if or lt c 10 gt c 30
gt_xnum c
ret
end
i = sub c 10
s = ulong get q_co i
for j ulong ulong get q_cl i bound 64
gt_xc ulong get q_cn add s j
end
end
note scratch file word w holds exactly the line in q_ex
fn gt_xok w ulong to bool
gt_ps w
if not gt_slurp 2
ret false
end
n = get q_n 21
if ne get q_n 6 n
ret false
end
for j ulong n bound 4096
if ne get q_b2 j get q_ex j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note scratch file word w is empty
fn gt_nil w ulong to bool
gt_ps w
if not gt_slurp 2
ret false
end
ret eq get q_n 6 0
end
note the one refusal line of tool t (2 ngcheck, 3 ngas, 4 ngdis, 5 ng, 6 ngrun) for exit ex at off (IR.md s10, s11)
fn gt_refx t ulong ex ulong off ulong to void
gt_xclr
if eq t 3
if eq ex 23
gt_xs 31
else
gt_xs 30
end
gt_xnum off
gt_xc 10
ret
end
if eq t 2
gt_xs 27
gt_xcn ex
else
if eq t 4
gt_xs 28
else
gt_xs gt_rpre t
end
gt_xnum ex
end
gt_xs 32
gt_xnum off
gt_xc 10
end
fn gt_rpre t ulong to ulong
if eq t 6
ret 92
end
ret 29
end
note a refusal: scratch err is exactly the refusal line and stdout (scratch word o) is empty
fn gt_refok t ulong ex ulong off ulong o ulong to bool
gt_refx t ex off
if not gt_xok 21
gt_fail0 38
ret false
end
if not gt_nil o
gt_fail0 39
ret false
end
ret true
end
note an acceptance: scratch out is exactly "ACCEPT <sha256 of b1[0, n)> fns=F blocks=B ops=O\n" with
note the counts the gate took from the fixture text (q_n 22..24), and scratch err is empty
fn gt_witok n ulong to void
for j ulong n bound 16777216
put sh_dat j get q_b1 j
end
sh_all n
gt_xclr
gt_xs 33
for j ulong 32
x = ulong get sh_dig j
gt_xc ulong get q_hex shr x 4
gt_xc ulong get q_hex and x 15
end
gt_xs 34
gt_xnum get q_n 22
gt_xs 35
gt_xnum get q_n 23
gt_xs 36
gt_xnum get q_n 24
gt_xc 10
if not gt_xok 20
gt_fail0 37
ret
end
if not gt_nil 21
gt_fail0 37
end
end
note fixture counts from its text in b2: functions (lines "fn ", "export ", "kernel "), blocks (lines
note "block " inside a function), ops (every other nonempty line inside a function but "end")
fn gt_tcount to void
put q_n 22 0
put q_n 23 0
put q_n 24 0
inf = false
s = ulong 0
for p ulong get q_n 6 bound 16777216
if eq get q_b2 p 10
inf = gt_tline s p inf
s = add p 1
end
end
end
fn gt_tline s ulong e ulong inf bool to bool
if gt_tfn s e
put q_n 22 add get q_n 22 1
ret true
end
if not inf
ret false
end
if eq sub e s 3
if gt_tpre s e 52
ret false
end
end
if gt_tpre s e 51
put q_n 23 add get q_n 23 1
ret true
end
if gt e s
put q_n 24 add get q_n 24 1
end
ret true
end
fn gt_tfn s ulong e ulong to bool
if gt_tpre s e 48
ret true
end
if gt_tpre s e 49
ret true
end
ret gt_tpre s e 50
end
note line b2[s, e) starts with message i
fn gt_tpre s ulong e ulong i ulong to bool
k = ulong get q_ml i
if lt sub e s k
ret false
end
m = ulong get q_mo i
for j ulong k bound 64
if ne get q_b2 add s j get q_m add m j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note assemble fixture [a, b) into scratch bin; false (case failed) when ngas refuses
fn gt_asm a ulong b ulong to bool
gt_pfix a b
x = gt_tool 3 23
if ne x 0
gt_failv 4 x
ret false
end
ret true
end
note T NAME EXIT OFFSET
fn gt_tcase to void
a = gt_name
b = get q_n 19
ex = gt_dec
off = gt_dec
if not gt_asm a b
ret
end
gt_ps 23
x = gt_tool 4 24
if ne x 0
gt_failv 5 x
ret
end
gt_ps 24
if not gt_slurp 1
gt_fail0 21
ret
end
gt_pfix a b
if not gt_slurp 2
gt_fail0 21
ret
end
gt_tcount
if not gt_same
gt_fail0 6
end
gt_ps 23
gt_verdict 2 ex off
gt_ps 23
if not gt_slurp 1
gt_fail0 21
ret
end
n = get q_n 5
if eq ex 0
if eq get q_n 12 0
gt_witok n
end
end
gt_ngchk n ex off
end
note run tool t (ngcheck 2 or ngdis 4) on the path in q_pa: exit ex, and for a refusal its one line
fn gt_verdict t ulong ex ulong off ulong to void
x = gt_tool t 20
if ne x ex
if eq t 2
gt_failv 7 x
else
gt_failv 20 x
end
ret
end
if ne ex 0
s = gt_refok t ex off 20
end
end
note the classes every reader refuses alike, at the same offset (IR.md s14)
fn gt_strict c ulong to bool
if or eq c 10 or eq c 11 eq c 12
ret true
end
if or eq c 14 or eq c 15 eq c 23
ret true
end
ret eq c 27
end
note ng ir-copy of the unit b1[0, n) that ngcheck judged ex at off: for a structural class (gt_strict)
note the same refusal line; otherwise the same bytes out, or (ngcheck refused) a refusal of its own
fn gt_ngchk n ulong ex ulong off ulong to void
gt_ps 26
if not gt_spill n
gt_fail0 21
ret
end
k = gt_pre n
gt_ps 22
if not gt_spill add n k
gt_fail0 21
ret
end
gt_ps 22
x = gt_tool 5 20
gt_ngv x ex off
end
note put "@ng ir-copy\n" before b1[0, n); its length
fn gt_pre n ulong to ulong
k = len q_irc
for j ulong n bound 16777216
put q_b1 sub add n k add 1 j get q_b1 sub n add 1 j
end
for j ulong k bound 16
put q_b1 j get q_irc j
end
ret k
end
note judge ng's exit x (stdout scratch out, the unit in scratch unit) against ngcheck's ex at off
fn gt_ngv x ulong ex ulong off ulong to void
if gt_strict ex
if ne x ex
gt_failv 40 x
ret
end
s = gt_refok 5 ex off 20
ret
end
if eq x 0
if not gt_fcmp 26 20
gt_fail0 11
end
ret
end
if eq ex 0
gt_failv 10 x
ret
end
if or lt x 10 gt x 30
gt_failv 40 x
ret
end
if not gt_nil 20
gt_fail0 39
end
end
note S NAME LINE
fn gt_scase to void
a = gt_name
b = get q_n 19
ln = gt_dec
gt_pfix a b
x = gt_tool 3 23
if ne x 3
gt_failv 4 x
ret
end
s = gt_refok 3 3 ln 23
end
note M BASE POS BYTE EXIT OFF / C BASE LEN EXIT OFF / A BASE BYTE EXIT OFF
fn gt_mcase k ulong to void
a = gt_name
b = get q_n 19
p = gt_dec
v = ulong 0
if eq k 77
v = gt_dec
end
ex = gt_dec
off = gt_dec
if not gt_asm a b
ret
end
